   "evidence": "`mathlib/Mathlib/Order/Filter/Finite.lean:252` `eventually_all_finite {I : Set \u03b9} (hI : I.Finite) : (\u2200\u1da0 x in l, \u2200 i \u2208 I, p i x) \u2194 \u2200 i \u2208 I, \u2200\u1da0 x in l, p i x`, with `:256` `alias Set.Finite.eventually_all`; `mathlib/Mathlib/Order/Filter/AtTopBot/Basic.lean:79` `eventually_atTop : (\u2200\u1da0 x in atTop, p x) \u2194 \u2203 a, \u2200 b, a \u2264 b \u2192 p b` (`@[to_dual]`, so `eventually_atBot` exists); `mathlib/Mathlib/Data/Set/Finite/Basic.lean:410` `List.finite_toSet (l : List \u03b1) : {x | x \u2208 l}.Finite`. `R` is a linear ordered field, hence `Nonempty` and directed, so `eventually_atTop` applies.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Polynomial/Eval/Infinity.lean",
   "fix": "Prove both from Mathlib: `Filter.eventually_atTop.1 (cs.finite_toSet.eventually_all.2 fun p _ => Filter.eventually_atTop.2 \u27e8B + 1, ...\u27e9)` using `exists_sign_atTop p` (dually `Filter.eventually_atBot` for the `atBot` case). The existing \u2203B statements can stay unchanged; only the induction bodies disappear.",
   "issue": "`List.exists_signs_atTop` (line 99) and `List.exists_signs_atBot` (line 112) are two hand-rolled `max`/`min` inductions producing a uniform bound for a finite family \u2014 exactly the finite-conjunction-of-eventually combinator Mathlib already provides.",
   "line": "99"
  }
 ],
